1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,440
In order to scan a website you first need to add it to BurpSuite Enterprise.

2
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:13,320
Adding a site's details makes it possible to take full advantage of BurpSuite Enterprise's

3
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:18,560
analytics features which enable you to track issues with your site over time.

4
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:24,680
Most of BurpSuite Enterprise's data and configuration options are managed on a per site basis.

5
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:27,920
Now you can add as many sites as you wish at no extra cost.

6
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:32,040
BurpSuite Enterprise Edition licensing is based around the number of concurrent scans

7
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:37,120
that you can run and not the number of sites added to the system.

8
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:40,240
Please also note that your scanning machine must be able to access the site that you want

9
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:45,360
to scan and for more information on allowing access please see our documentation configuring

10
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:47,880
your environment network and firewall settings.

11
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:53,300
Okay to begin with we navigate to our sites page and in the top right corner we'll see

12
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:55,880
the new site button.

13
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,160
Here we can add the site details so we want to give it a unique name.

14
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:04,380
In this case we'll just call it test and then we can add it to one of our folders.

15
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:08,940
If we leave this at the default root folder the site is created at the top level of the site

16
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:11,060
tree.

17
00:01:11,060 --> 00:01:13,000
Next we can add our site scope.

18
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:18,000
So firstly this is going to be the highest level URL that we want to include in scans of

19
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,280
this site and all sub directories of that URL will be scanned by default.

20
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:25,560
So we can add our URL in.

21
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:30,700
This is PortsWigger's deliberately vulnerable test web application which you are free to

22
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:34,180
use for the purposes of your own testing.

23
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:40,140
So by default this is going to be scanned using HTTP and HTTPS or if we were to specify

24
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:46,600
a protocol in the URL we can select scan using my specified protocol just to pick one of those.

25
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:51,880
If we expand the additional options here for site scope we'll see an option for included

26
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:54,880
URLs and excluded URLs.

27
00:01:54,880 --> 00:02:00,680
So for included URLs if there are URLs that are part of the same web application but not

28
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:05,880
contained under the specified site URL we can add it here to bring it into our scope for the

29
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:06,880
scan.

30
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:12,720
In contrast if there's elements of the application that we do not want to scan we can add that

31
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:19,400
to the excluded URLs list and that will be skipped during the scan.

32
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:21,280
Now we can move on to our site settings.

33
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:25,640
So firstly that's going to be our scan configuration that's used for the scans against this particular

34
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:28,820
application and we have two options here.

35
00:02:28,820 --> 00:02:34,060
We can use the preset scan mode designed to get you up and running as quick as possible and

36
00:02:34,060 --> 00:02:38,940
this ranges from a lightweight scan which will be completed within 15 minutes all the way

37
00:02:38,940 --> 00:02:44,280
to deep which is going to get better coverage and understanding of the site security posture

38
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:48,460
but that will take longer in terms of the scan time.

39
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:52,300
If we want to create a custom configuration we can do so and add it to our library and that

40
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:54,000
will be accessible here.

41
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:59,020
There are also some built-in custom configurations that you can utilize out of the box and this

42
00:02:59,020 --> 00:03:03,960
just changes the behavior of either the crawl or the audit in some way shape or form.

43
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:09,720
So perhaps we're limiting the crawl maximizing the audit doing something like a minimization

44
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:16,840
of false positives but you can also create your own enough complete control over those custom options.

45
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:20,840
Those are the required settings.

46
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:26,360
The remaining scan settings are optional but can be useful to get the most out of your scan.

47
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:32,120
So for example if we wanted to add authentication to our scan we can do so here.

48
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:34,120
Option one being a username and password.

49
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:40,360
So if you've got quite a basic single page login mechanism we can give it a label, add our username,

50
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:46,120
add our password and we locate that form during the scan or submit those credentials.

51
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:50,360
For anything more complex we would recommend our recorded login sequence.

52
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:56,440
You can learn about how this works with the link in product to the documentation but once you've got

53
00:03:56,440 --> 00:04:02,840
that set up and recorded it'll generate a JSON file which is a sequence of events for logging in that the

54
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:06,120
crawler can follow and you can paste that here.

55
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:12,760
This is typically for anything more complex than a single form so single sign-on or multi-page login for example.

56
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:19,880
We can also specify our extensions. Extensions are available through the Burp BAP store.

57
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:23,400
Once added to your enterprise installation they'll be selectable from the list

58
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:28,040
and typically extensions will modify the behavior of the crawler in some way shape or form.

59
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:34,600
And finally if we set up a scanning pool which includes a dedicated scanning machine resource

60
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:39,160
we can allocate that here but by default it will just be added to the default pool.

61
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:46,520
Once we've set all our options we can click save and our site has been created.

62
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:52,280
We can then perform a pre-scan check which will perform a connection check against the provided URL

63
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:57,800
and give us a result and also if we added a recorded login sequence that will be replayed

64
00:04:57,800 --> 00:05:00,360
and checked to ensure that we've logged in okay.

65
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:05,800
Now that your site has been created you can move on to running your first scan.

66
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:14,440
Please note that we recommend keeping a consistent scan configuration for each site that you add.

67
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:18,920
Changing the scan configuration can affect vulnerability trends over time

68
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:23,320
and cause Burp BAPS to Enterprise Edition to give inaccurate time estimates when scanning.

69
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:28,920
If you want to scan a site that you've already added with a new configuration we would recommend adding the

70
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:35,240
site again with the new configuration selected because as mentioned we don't limit the number of sites that you create.

71
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:45,240
Thank you.

